Memo for Record: The data below drove the decision to use gzip=1 + shuffle for the code's compressed data files. 
The "size %" column was the most important factor, since the goal was to reduce file size as much as possible 
while keeping read/write times reasonable. gzip=1 + shuffle provided a 40% reduction in size compared to the 
uncompressed baseline, which was a significant improvement. The write time of 17.854 seconds and read time of 3.137 
seconds were also acceptable for our use case, especially considering the large size of the original data (2155.30 MB). 
Higher gzip levels (like gzip=9) did not provide much additional compression but significantly increased write times,
making them less practical for our needs. 

